      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, when a plugin returns a subclass of `PluginDefinedInfo`.\n\nThe base DTO has only `name` and `message`, but the extension point explicitly allows plugins to subclass it. This is covered by tests too: `ChangeMetaIT` defines `MyMetaHash extends PluginDefinedInfo` with an extra `myMetaRef` field and asserts that the REST response contains it as `my_meta_ref`.\n\nI’ll clarify the text so the table is described as the common/base fields, while plugin-specific subclasses may add additional fields.",
